; An element may carry a keymap that views:keymap-mark names; a click in
; it looks the mouse key up there before every keymap at its position.
; The page sends the keymaps of the marked elements from the one clicked
; out, innermost first, each by the number before the mark's state.
> (define-table close-keys)
> (commands:define-command (on-close [event (keys:command-event)])
    "Records a click on a close button."
